  "body": "## What changed\nOperation, setup and tool names were already cleaned by each post's `clean()` (#257), but the **machine name in the program header was written raw**. Five shipped machine files have parentheses in their names (`Tormach 770MX (ML)`, `Tormach PCNC 1100 (Series I/II/3)`, `Tormach PCNC 770 (Series 3)`), so their headers posted a nested comment such as `(Tormach 770MX (ML))`, which LinuxCNC/PathPilot refuses. Hand-edited machine names (#478's editor) could break any dialect the same way.\n- **The six affected posts:** the header name now goes through the post's own `clean()`, with a fallback of `CAMCRAFT` if nothing is left.\n- **Tormach:** `note()` also guards against LinuxCNC active comments. A text starting with `MSG`, `DEBUG`, `PRINT`, `LOG*`, `PROBEOPEN`/`PROBECLOSE`, `ABORT`, `AXIS` or `PY*` (any case, whole word) is prefixed with `- `, so a user's name never becomes an operator message or a log command.\n- **Engine default:** `writeComment()` (js.rs) turns `(`, `)` and control characters into spaces.\n- **Rules:**\n  - `( )` dialects (Fanuc, Fanuc lathe, Haas, Mazak, Tormach; RS-274 / ISO 6983): `( ) % ;` become spaces, non-printable or non-ASCII characters become `?`, runs of spaces collapse, 40-character cap.\n  - Sinumerik: `;` comments get the same `clean()`.\n  - Heidenhain: already safe; it is now tested.\n- **Not done:** no uppercasing, so existing goldens stay byte-identical. Parentheses become spaces rather than `[ ]`, because brackets are expression syntax on macro B and LinuxCNC.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/594-comment-escape.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `comment_escape`:**\n  - `hostile_names_post_well_formed_comments_in_every_mill_dialect`: machine `MSG, Mill (A); B*`, op `Op (1); debug*`, tool `EM(6);*`. Every line holds at most one balanced comment closed at the end of the line, with no `;` and ASCII only. Tormach writes no active comment, and the Sinumerik and Heidenhain block rules hold.\n  - `hostile_names_post_well_formed_comments_on_the_lathe`.\n  - `every_bundled_machine_name_posts_a_single_header_comment`: every shipped Tormach .mch.\n  - All three failed before the change.\n- **Gate:** the 25 post-related app suites (conformance, golden_cl, posting, and every post, lathe, inverted, coolant and comment suite) and all camcraft-post tests pass. Clippy is clean. **No golden changed.**\n\nChangelog: Posts clean the machine name in the program header like every other comment (no nested \"(...)\" from names such as \"Tormach 770MX (ML)\"), and the Tormach post never writes a user name as a LinuxCNC active comment (MSG/DEBUG/PRINT/LOG...) (#594)\n\nFixes #594\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
